  "id": "eef58d0f-b7d0-481e-b3f6-bb20cd597dce",
  "title": "IndiGo, Air India shift flights to Navi Mumbai ahead of T1 revamp",
  "summary": "IndiGo and Air India Group plan to shift about a third of their international flights to Navi Mumbai airport as foreign carriers continue to oppose the proposed relocation, while the airline and Adani Airport Holdings Ltd (AAHL) prepare to expand international operations at the new airport in phases.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "IndiGo and Air India Group plan to shift 12 daily international departures from CSMIA to NMIA from February 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The transition, which is in the final stages of operational planning, will cover IndiGo's existing services from CSMIA to NMIA, enabling passengers to connect between the airline's domestic and international flights.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "IndiGo will also introduce a daily service to Kathmandu, taking its international network at NMIA to 12 destinations between February and July 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
